<title>SPAIN: FORECAST - BBV Q1 profit to rise 24.2 pct.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - BBV Q1 profit to rise 24.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a consensus of analysts forecasts for BBV 1997 first quarter results.</p>
<p>			(billions of pesetas unless stated):</p>
<p> BBV			    Q1 .97     Q1. 96	Range</p>
<p> Net interest income	122.11     99.69   125.00 - 117.00</p>
<p> Operating margin	    69.61     54.40    76.80 -  65.00</p>
<p> Net attributable	    24.61     19.81    25.10 -  24.10</p>
<p>Contributors: AB Asesores, Merrill Lynch, Inverban, Central Hispano Bolsa, Benito y Monjardin, Ahorro Corporacion, ABN AMRO.</p>
<p>NOTE: BBV will announce 1997 Q1 results on April 17.</p>
